<title>JAPAN: Japan May retail sales fall 1.8%, overall sales up.</title>
<headline>Japan May retail sales fall 1.8%, overall sales up.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's retail sales fell 1.8 percent in May from a year earlier, falling for the second month in a row, the Ministry of International Trade and Industry said on Friday.</p>
<p>Overall sales increased 1.7 percent from a year earlier.</p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of the figures:</p>
<p>    (Year-on-year)	  MAY				  APR</p>
<p>    Overall		  +1.7 pct (51.79 trln yen)    -1.4 pct</p>
<p>    Retail		   -1.8 pct (11.54 trln yen)    -4.2 pct</p>
<p>     large-scale stores  -3.3 pct (1.81 trln yen)     -8.1 pct</p>
<p>    Wholesale		+2.8 pct (40.25 trln yen)    -0.6 pct</p>
<p>Note: Large-scale stores refers to department stores and supermarkets, while the retail sales category also includes car dealerships and smaller stores.</p>
